WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.058
All right, this is an overview for how to do the learning

00:00:04.108 --> 00:00:06.148
period to model a muscle lab.

00:00:06.198 --> 00:00:07.950
So, you should have a bag

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.327
full of straws and tape. And that is what you will need

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:14.950
to do this lab. And then you should also have your skeletal

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.502
muscle model open, the document, so that way you're able to record

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.571
things along while you go. So,

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.950
to start out, if you

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.488
did receive spaghetti noodles, then the first step you're going to do

00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:28.540
is you're going to take all your straws,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.950
take the spaghetti noodles, and you're going to

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.599
like fill them all. So, if you just have a stack of

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.301
straws, and you just like drop spaghetti noodles in,

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:38.950
it'll start putting them inside, and it should be a

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.236
pretty quick process. If you do not have that,

00:00:42.286 --> 00:00:46.307
don't worry about it. Just go ahead and move to step two.

00:00:46.357 --> 00:00:49.950
So, step one is to fill your straws with spaghetti.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.950
The spaghetti noodles that go inside represent the myofilaments.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.674
All right. Um, and they are all bundled inside of a myofibril.

00:00:59.724 --> 00:01:02.950
So, these individual straws are myofibrils.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.516
All right. So, if you don't have those,

00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:08.871
like I said, just go ahead and move on to step two.

00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:12.950
So, for step two, you're going to gather seven myofibrils like

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.988
so. It'll kind of look like a little bit of a flower.

00:01:16.038 --> 00:01:18.969
And then you're going to take a small piece of tape.

00:01:19.019 --> 00:01:21.950
So, this is just kind of like the method that worked

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.614
for me. Whatever method works for you is cool,

00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:30.313
but I found it really helpful to start by grabbing my seven

00:01:30.363 --> 00:01:30.950
and just

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.535
taping the top of all of them to start so that it

00:01:34.585 --> 00:01:38.852
was kind of like they were already bundled and ready to go.

00:01:38.902 --> 00:01:39.950
All right. Once

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.682
you do that with all the groups of seven,

00:01:41.732 --> 00:01:42.950
you might have some left over.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.716
For example, I have one left over.

00:01:44.766 --> 00:01:46.950
So, I'm just going to put that to the side.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.646
But once you have all of those,

00:01:49.696 --> 00:01:52.950
then you're going to go ahead and take

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.950
that same color masking tape. And this tape represents your endomysium.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.950
So it's the layer that is wrapping around these

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.950
um these myofibrils. Okay.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.981
So, I'm going to just go ahead and show you how I

00:02:17.031 --> 00:02:18.639
wrap it. It might be as you're wrapping,

00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:20.297
you might get a little bubble like that,

00:02:20.347 --> 00:02:21.997
that's okay. Just kind of squish it down.

00:02:22.047 --> 00:02:22.950
But if you're just kind

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.216
of keeping it at an angle and wrapping close around,

00:02:28.266 --> 00:02:30.950
it should work pretty well.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.354
And you do have pretty much just enough tape on this.

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:37.822
The whatever tape you use first is going to run out or

00:02:37.872 --> 00:02:37.950
be

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.104
close to running out. Um, but you have just enough to be

00:02:40.154 --> 00:02:40.950
able to wrap them all.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.540
As you can see off to the side here,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.842
I already have them all wrapped.

00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:49.943
Um, so you're going to repeat that process for all of the

00:02:49.993 --> 00:02:50.950
muscle fibers.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.637
So, at this step, make sure to take a picture of your

00:02:54.687 --> 00:02:57.698
muscle fiber, um, or all your muscle fibers.

00:02:57.748 --> 00:02:58.950
So, you can have a

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.479
picture of all of them or you can hold them up to

00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:03.389
the camera and show them off and say,

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:05.144
"These are the muscle fibers." So,

00:03:05.194 --> 00:03:06.950
next up, we're making our fascicle.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.950
So, I'm going to take three groupings.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.371
way. There we go. So, three different groupings and do them in

00:03:13.421 --> 00:03:16.460
bundles of three. Once again, I'm going to do a piece of

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.950
tape to start. That'll make

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.450
life easier. And then I'm going to go ahead and just kind

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.871
of do that top again so that they kind of stick together

00:03:26.921 --> 00:03:26.950
a

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.780
little bit better as I'm trying to manipulate these.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.664
If you have a friend or a family member that you want

00:03:32.714 --> 00:03:34.732
to help you with this on just holding,

00:03:34.782 --> 00:03:34.950
that

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.703
might be helpful. But you can see I can do it without

00:03:37.753 --> 00:03:39.314
having any support as well. So,

00:03:39.364 --> 00:03:41.184
I'm going to go through and do that.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.950
You can do the other side as well.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:51.283
And then, um, I do want you to go through and wrap

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:51.950
your

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.027
fascicles with their perimysium. So, same thing.

00:03:55.077 --> 00:03:58.232
Um, you're just going to kind of slowly go around.

00:03:58.282 --> 00:04:01.950
You can see mine's actually overlapping a little too much.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.753
So, I'm just going to kind of undo and redo.

00:04:04.803 --> 00:04:07.874
So, it's okay if some of the green shows through,

00:04:07.924 --> 00:04:11.950
but know that if this was an actual muscle that perimysium would

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.950
cover all of those bundles of muscle fibers.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.407
Keep going all the way down.

00:04:20.457 --> 00:04:24.851
You see, it's not a perfect process,

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.950
but it does work.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:35.950
So now we have our bundle of muscle fibers creating our fascicle.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.897
Okay, right here we are. I have all of my,

00:04:38.947 --> 00:04:42.476
uh, fascicles that are wrapped in their perimysium.

00:04:42.526 --> 00:04:43.950
And now our next step

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.883
is to take all of our fascicles and bundle them together to

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:48.950
make our muscle.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.761
Uh, also as a note, I did have two bundles that were

00:04:51.811 --> 00:04:54.139
left over that didn't make a group of three,

00:04:54.189 --> 00:04:55.545
so I just put it in there.

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.950
And now I can do that next

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.359
step. So, same thing. I'm going to just pull off a large

00:05:00.409 --> 00:05:03.950
thing of tape first just to kind of bundle it all together.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.335
Sorry. There we go. And I'll show you in just...

00:05:06.385 --> 00:05:08.074
And so, if you're doing this alone,

00:05:08.124 --> 00:05:10.907
I think what's probably going to be the easiest is to put

00:05:10.957 --> 00:05:11.950
a large thing of tape

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:17.318
down and then just to kind of put them on there and

00:05:17.368 --> 00:05:19.950
then kind of squish those

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.018
other ones in there as you go.

00:05:23.068 --> 00:05:28.950
So if you like have them stacked and then you can probably

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.950
put this on there and this one there.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.918
Just trying to make do with what we have by just having

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:41.989
only myself being able to wrap it.

00:05:42.039 --> 00:05:47.589
But if you have someone, you're welcome to have them help you,

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:47.950
too.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.950
Okay. So there is my muscle,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.176
my full muscle. And I'm going to go ahead and wrap the

00:05:56.226 --> 00:05:59.150
whole thing, um, in the outside layer,

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.950
which is our epimysium.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.765
All right. And there we go.

00:06:02.815 --> 00:06:05.320
It's all the way wrapped. Here we are.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.547
So, this is our muscle wrapped in our epimysium.

00:06:08.597 --> 00:06:08.950
And we

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.218
can go through and still see all of those different parts.

00:06:12.268 --> 00:06:14.189
So, thinking back to the beginning,

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:16.950
we had the myofilaments would have been the pasta

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.306
that's inside. Each one of the straws is a myofibril.

00:06:21.356 --> 00:06:25.991
We bundled the straws together to make our muscle fibers.

00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:28.950
They were wrapped in our endomysium.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.206
And then we took lots of muscle fibers,

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:33.115
or three groups of muscle fibers,

00:06:33.165 --> 00:06:35.950
but lots of muscle fibers, grouped them together.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.164
And we made a fascicle. And the fascicle was wrapped in the

00:06:40.214 --> 00:06:40.950
perimysium.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.381
And then we took all of our fascicles and bundled them together

00:06:46.431 --> 00:06:50.950
and wrapped them in our epimysium to make our muscle.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.152
So, make sure to add your pictures to the document and then

00:06:54.202 --> 00:06:56.159
finish the questions. And that's all.

00:06:56.209 --> 00:06:57.950
Let me know if you need any help.
